To run an asynchronous task in the `beforeEach` hook, accept a `next` callback as a second argument. Wrap your async code in a `try/catch/finally` block and call `next(markdown)` when ready:

```
hook.beforeEach((markdown, next) => {
  try {
    // Async task(s)...
  } catch (err) {
    // ...
  } finally {
    next(markdown);
  }
});
```

This prevents errors from affecting docsify and other plugins.

